ed residue: /tmp/dracut.log and /tmp/reboot.log, which are direct low-risk byproducts of the dracut rebuild and background reboot trigger, not abandoned experiments. No failed services, no unexpected listening-socket changes beyond PID renumbering from the reboot, and no destructive or unrelated mutations were found in the executor timeline.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-339a303ebff44ff5\",\"cmd-0e120c25fb6549da\",\"global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files\",\"global:after_executor:node1:failed-services\",\"global:before_prepare:node1:temporary-files\"]},\"overall_summary\":\"The executor blacklisted usb-storage via /etc/modprobe.d and an install-to-/bin/false override, rebuilt the initramfs so the block applies at early boot, and directly demonstrated both immediate blocking (before reboot) and persistence across an actual reboot cycle with a verified change in boot identity and post-reboot confirmation that the module remains blocked. Both material outcomes of the task are satisfied with direct, first-hand evidence rather than configuration alone.\",\"limitations\":[\"Package-health checks were unavailable (timed out) in both lifecycle snapshots, so native package-manager consistency could not be independently verified, though this is unrelated to the task's material outcomes.\",\"No further reboot cycles were captured beyond the single mandatory restart, so long-term persistence across multiple future reboots is inferred from the initramfs rebuild plus one successful reboot rather than directly observed multiple times.\"]}","structured_output":{"requirements":[{"id":"immediate-block","requirement":"Stop usb-storage kernel module from loading now (immediate effect)","status":"satisfied","summary":"Baseline confirmed usb-storage was not loaded and no prior blacklist existed (cmd-02e91ddd8e394736, cmd-a135dbb450b24443, cmd-24d994c62cbf4e75). Created /etc/modprobe.d/usb-storage-blacklist.conf with 'blacklist usb-storage' and 'install usb-storage /bin/false' (cmd-2c606